Modules generated by select dependencies must be visible to other stanzas in
the same directory.
Regression test for https://github.com/ocaml/dune/issues/14085.

  $ make_dune_project 3.21
  $ cat > dune <<'EOF'
  > (library
  >  (name mylib)
  >  (modules :standard \ myexe myexe_select))
  > (executable
  >  (name myexe)
  >  (modules myexe myexe_select)
  >  (libraries mylib
  >   (select myexe_select.ml from
  >    (-> myexe_select.fallback.ml))))
  > EOF
  $ echo 'let message = "selected"' > mylib.ml
  $ echo 'let () = print_endline Myexe_select.message' > myexe.ml
  $ echo 'let message = Mylib.message' > myexe_select.fallback.ml

The library should be able to exclude the executable's selected module.

  $ dune exec ./myexe.exe
  selected

The reverse layout also needs to work: the executable excludes modules selected
by the library, including a selected interface.

  $ cat > dune <<'EOF'
  > (library
  >  (name mylib)
  >  (modules mylib mylib_select)
  >  (libraries
  >   (select mylib_select.ml from (-> mylib_select.fallback.ml))
  >   (select mylib_select.mli from (-> mylib_select.fallback.mli))))
  > (executable
  >  (name myexe)
  >  (modules :standard \ mylib mylib_select)
  >  (libraries mylib))
  > EOF
  $ echo 'let message = Mylib_select.message' > mylib.ml
  $ echo 'let () = print_endline Mylib.message' > myexe.ml
  $ echo 'let message = "selected library"' > mylib_select.fallback.ml
  $ echo 'val message : string' > mylib_select.fallback.mli
  $ dune exec ./myexe.exe
  selected library

Selections in test stanzas also participate in an unqualified directory group.

  $ mkdir sub
  $ cat > dune <<'EOF'
  > (include_subdirs unqualified)
  > (library
  >  (name mylib)
  >  (modules :standard \ myexe myexe_select))
  > (test
  >  (name myexe)
  >  (modules myexe myexe_select)
  >  (libraries mylib
  >   (select sub/myexe_select.ml from
  >    (-> sub/myexe_select.fallback.ml))))
  > EOF
  $ echo 'let message = "selected test"' > mylib.ml
  $ echo 'let () = print_endline Myexe_select.message' > myexe.ml
  $ mv myexe_select.fallback.ml sub/
  $ dune runtest
  selected test

Qualified module paths must refer to selected sources as well.

  $ make_dune_project 3.25
  $ cat > dune <<'EOF'
  > (include_subdirs qualified)
  > (library
  >  (name mylib)
  >  (modules :standard \ myexe Sub.Myexe_select))
  > (executable
  >  (name myexe)
  >  (modules myexe Sub.Myexe_select)
  >  (libraries mylib
  >   (select sub/myexe_select.ml from
  >    (-> sub/myexe_select.fallback.ml))))
  > EOF
  $ echo 'let () = print_endline Sub.Myexe_select.message' > myexe.ml
  $ dune exec ./myexe.exe
  selected test

Disabled stanzas must not contribute selected modules to their neighbors.

  $ cat > dune <<'EOF'
  > (library
  >  (name mylib)
  >  (modules :standard \ myexe))
  > (executable
  >  (name myexe)
  >  (enabled_if false)
  >  (modules myexe missing)
  >  (libraries
  >   (select missing.ml from (-> missing.fallback.ml))))
  > EOF
  $ dune build mylib.cma

Selected modules must also be included in another stanza's :standard, even
when the stanza declaring the select does not compile those modules itself.

  $ mkdir standard
  $ cd standard
  $ make_dune_project 3.21
  $ cat > dune <<'EOF'
  > (library
  >  (name generator)
  >  (modules)
  >  (libraries
  >   (select selected.ml from (-> selected.fallback.ml))
  >   (select selected.mli from (-> selected.fallback.mli))))
  > (executable
  >  (name main)
  >  (modules :standard))
  > EOF
  $ echo 'let () = print_endline Selected.message' > main.ml
  $ echo 'let message = "selected from :standard"' > selected.fallback.ml
  $ echo 'val message : string' > selected.fallback.mli
  $ dune exec ./main.exe
  selected from :standard

Omitting the modules field must use the same default module set.

  $ cat > dune <<'EOF'
  > (library
  >  (name generator)
  >  (modules)
  >  (libraries
  >   (select selected.ml from (-> selected.fallback.ml))
  >   (select selected.mli from (-> selected.fallback.mli))))
  > (executable
  >  (name main))
  > EOF
  $ dune exec ./main.exe
  selected from :standard
